.TH FILESERVER 1 "April 2026" "fileserver" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
fileserver - serve static files using configuration from an envdir directory

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fileserver
.RI [ DIR ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fileserver
is a small example program included with
.BR envdir .
It optionally reads environment settings from
.I DIR
and serves files over HTTP.

If
.I DIR
is omitted, the program uses
.BR ./env .

If
.I DIR
does not exist, the program falls back to the current process environment and
its built-in defaults. Other errors while reading
.I DIR
cause the program to exit with an error.

.SH ENVIRONMENT

The program recognizes these variables:

.TP
.B SERVER_HOST
Host or IP address to bind.
Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1 .

.TP
.B SERVER_PORT
TCP port to listen on.
Default:
.BR 8080 .

.TP
.B SERVER_DIR
Directory to serve.
Default:
.BR . .

.SH EXAMPLES

Serve files using the example envdir:

.nf
fileserver ./examples/fileserver/env
.fi

Serve the current directory on port 9000 without an envdir:

.nf
SERVER_PORT=9000 SERVER_DIR=. fileserver ./missing-envdir
.fi

Run the example through
.BR envdir :

.nf
envdir ./examples/fileserver/env fileserver
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS

The program exits with status 0 on success.
Configuration or server startup errors cause a non-zero exit status.

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR envdir (1)

.SH AUTHOR

Example program in the
.B envdir
repository.

Mat Kovach
